differs now fails fast' and check_uv_pin.py:_is_exact_specifier both treat required-version as ==-only, so a range value is a NEW usage of the key for this repo","Plan's 'Lock churn: none' evidence was measured 'On a scratch copy, uv 0.12.7 and uv 0.13.6 both pass `uv lock --check`' — i.e. with the == pin, not with a >= floor","The only AC that exercises the range value ('uv lock --check exits 0 under uv 0.13.6') runs after implementation","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — the required-version field is a known uv feature, but the specific surface (accepting a >= range) is unconfirmed in the plan"],"finding":"The plan's entire fix depends on uv's [tool.uv] required-version key accepting a PEP 440 RANGE specifier (>=0.12.7), but the plan never records verifying that capability against uv --help/docs or a live run; its empirical evidence (scratch-copy uv lock --check passing under 0.12.7 and 0.13.6) was gathered against the existing ==0.13.6 pin and only confirms lock byte-identity, not that uv accepts >= in required-version.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd74b33f746dea06","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / pyproject.toml:362","norm_id":"n36736015dd3145ac","priority":0.3056,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If uv rejects a non-exact required-version (e.g. parses only ==), uv lock --check and every uv invocation exit 2 the same way the == pin fails Dependabot, and the fix regresses CI instead of fixing Dependabot"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Before implementing, run uv (0.13.6 and 0.13.5) against a scratch pyproject carrying required-version = \">=0.12.7\" and confirm `uv lock --check` / `uv venv` exit 0; cite that observed result in the Evidence block, then reference it from AC 'uv lock --check exits 0 under uv 0.13.6'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_ab